The LICENSE and external scanner are from upstream tree-sitter/tree-sitter-ruby
at ad907a69da0c8a4f7a943a7fe012712208da6dee. This includes the upstream
heredoc serialization fix. Only a trailing blank line is removed from the license text.

Local changes in src/scanner.c recognize anonymous block forwarding before
a closing parenthesis across whitespace and line comments, and symbol labels
ending in '?' or '!', including Ruby's otherwise reserved 'defined?'.
A comma directly after an anonymous block argument is invalid in MRI; the
scanner now rejects it. The other examples in the upstream block-argument case
retain their original trees.
See crates/hoonarqube-ruby/src/tests/parser_syntax.rs for boundary tests.

grammar.js also accepts method bodies such as `def value! = raise Error, self`
and a rescue modifier on that call. The command starts with a plain argument;
operators, parenthesized arguments and blocks retain their existing grammar.
This bounded extension does not cover every Ruby command form. Generate the
parser, node types, grammar and headers from this directory with Tree-sitter
CLI 0.25.10: `tree-sitter generate --abi 14`. Runtime ABI remains 14.

The external scanner also accepts an equals delimiter after an explicit percent
literal type (for example %r=...=). Bare %= still belongs to modulo assignment.
